# Motivation

The output structure of flakes is quite unintuitive for most people. At best,
this creates a lot of boiler plate to be added to each project if you use utilities
like `flake-utils` or `flake-parts`. At worse, you are hardcoding attr paths with
embedded system types everywhere.

Since Ekapkgs embraces composition through overlays, in particular, abstractions
such as pkgsModules should enable arbitrary composition of package scopes easy.
For flakes, we can expose a `mkFlake` facade which should allow for people to
communicate their overlays and then they can provide system-agnostic projections
of the packages they desire.

# Detailed implementation

```nix
# For use with Ekapkgs repositories, prepend the pkgsModules from the repository
mkFlakeWith = pkgsModules: args: let
  allModules = pkgsModules ++ (args.pkgsModules or [ ]);
  newArgs = args // { pkgsModules = allModules; };
in mkFlake newArgs;

mkFlake = {
, pkgsModules ? [ ]
, packages ? null
, checks ? null
, apps ? null
, formatter ? null
, devShells ? null
, systems ? [ "x86_64-linux" "aarch64-linux" "aarch64-darwin" ]
# Doesn't get mapped over each system
, passthru
...
}: let
  forEachSystem = lib.genAttrs systems
  # This assumes that this is located in corepkgs' root directory
  pkgsForSystem = system: import ./. { inherit system pkgsModules; };
  # Evaluate legacyPackages as a fixed point to avoid re-instanting the package set each time
  legacyPackages = forEachSystem pkgsForSystem
  attrPredicate = name: value: value != null && lib.assertMsg (lib.isFunction value) "${name} must be a function"
  applyAttrFn = name: attrFn: pkgs: lib.optionalAttrs (attrPredicate name attrFn) { ${name} = attrFn pkgs; }
  applyAttrForSystem = name: attrFn: forEachSystem (system: applyAttrFn name attrFn legacyPackages.${system})
in
# TODO: make this not bad
{ packages = applyAttrForSystem "packages" packages; }
// { checks = applyAttrForSystem "checks" checks; }
// { apps = applyAttrForSystem "apps" apps; }
// { formatter = applyAttrForSystem "formatter" formatter; }
// { devShells = applyAttrForSystem "devShells" devShells; }
```



